  Let me verify the watchdog script and tunnel failover config quickly to ground the watchdog assessment. Check scripts/ for watchdog.Now check mgmt-tunnel-v3 init to see the endpoints and ports 18443-18447 mapping.Key finding: the watchdog probes only 18443 (primary endpoint local forward). When primary endpoint (DO→now DMIT) path degrades but backup tunnels (18444-18447) are alive, watchdog restarts the whole mgmt-tunnel service — killing healthy backup tunnels → restart storm. The v2 fix (probe 18443-18447, any healthy = no restart) matches the bug. Good, the plan's description of the fix is correct in direction.

  But wait — important subtlety: 18444-18447 are all -L forwards to the same MGMT_TARGET (DO hub 10.10.0.1:8443) via different relays. After Guangzhou switch, MGMT_TARGET=127.0.0.1:8443 relative to... MGMT_TARGET is evaluated on the VPS side — the -L target is resolved on the server. tunnel.conf in credential archive shows MGMT_TARGET=127.0.0.1:8443 for Guangzhou. But backup endpoints 2-5 still forward to... the same TC_MGMT_TARGET! Look at init script: backup endpoints use "$TC_MGMT_TARGET" too — so if you change MGMT_TARGET to 127.0.0.1:8443 (Guangzhou local), then backup tunnels via TX/BWG/66云 socat → DO sshd would forward to DO's 127.0.0.1:8443 — is there a service on DO:8443? DO is being retired. Hmm, previously MGMT_TARGET=10.10.0.1:8443 (WG hub on DO). Changing MGMT_TARGET to 127.0.0.1:8443 changes it for ALL endpoints including backups — the backup -L forwards terminate on different servers where 127.0.0.1:8443 means that server's local 8443. TX/BWG/66云 are socat relays to DO sshd, so their -L target is resolved on DO — DO:127.0.0.1:8443, does DO run the mgmt API on 8443? Probably the old management was on DO... DO retiring 11-02. So after switching MGMT_TARGET, backup legs may all point at DO:8443 which dies on 11-02. This is a real consistency gap: the plan/credential doc tunnel.conf template shows MGMT_TARGET=127.0.0.1:8443 without discussing what backup endpoints resolve to. Actually wait — for the Guangzhou primary, 127.0.0.1:8443 is correct. For backup legs terminating at DO (via socat), 127.0.0.1:8443 = DO's own 8443. Old config used 10.10.0.1:8443 (WG hub = DO itself). So probably DO:8443 hosts the mgmt API, so backups still work until 11-02, then die. The plan's item 4 (WG hub migration) relates: -L management channel goes through WG hub 10.10.0.1:8443... Hmm interesting: MGMT_TARGET=10.10.0.1:8443 means the -L forward goes over the WG network to hub. Credential doc known limitation #3: "DO 的 WG hub（10.10.0.1）尚未迁移，DO 退役后 -L 管理通道需改走广州或 GIA".

